he note \"A keeps calm in a crisis\" is in our notes. So we have evidence of stress resilience for A. Also \"A understands complicated technology\" is in notes, giving technical competence. So we have more evidence for A than previously considered. That strengthens A.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, but no decision quality, attention, adaptability, and nasty remarks. Also weak memory for numbers (attention). So B has gaps.\n\nThus we should shift to Candidate A. So our vote: Candidate A.\n\nWe need to produce public message: maybe agree with Agent 1 and 3, note new evidence: A keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology, which addresses stress resilience and technical competence. Also note that B lacks decision quality evidence. So we support A.\n\nThus produce public message: \"I concur with Agent 1 and 3, shift my recommendation to Candidate A because we have evidence of A's stress resilience and technical competence, while B lacks decision quality and attention evidence, and his interpersonal issue remains.\"\n\nProvide metadata JSON with vote Candidate A.\n\nProceed."}
